{Neo-Grünfeld Defense: Classical Variation, Modern Defense. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. O-O O-O {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. c4 dxc4 7. Na3 c3 8. bxc3 ! c5 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... Ne4 Rb1 Nd2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Re1 Nc6 10. Bb2 Qb6 11. Nc4 Qb5 ?! 12. Qb3 Qa6 13. Ncd2 Be6 14. Qa3 Qxa3 15. Bxa3 Nd7 16. Nb3 Bxb3 17. axb3 cxd4 18. cxd4 Nxd4 19. Nxd4 Bxd4 20. Rac1 Rac8 21. Bxb7 Rxc1 22. Rxc1 Rb8 23. Rc8+ Rxc8 24. Bxc8 Nc5 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} 25. e3 1-0
